1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:01,426
The shop door is open.

2
00:00:01,426 --> 00:00:02,614
You go through it.

3
00:00:02,614 --> 00:00:04,833
Just like the first evening,

4
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:05,769
except this time,

5
00:00:05,769 --> 00:00:08,304
you know exactly what you're walking into.

6
00:00:08,678 --> 00:00:10,114
Or you thought you did.

7
00:00:10,114 --> 00:00:11,966
The lights hum overhead.

8
00:00:11,966 --> 00:00:13,517
The fridge hums in the corner,

9
00:00:13,517 --> 00:00:16,272
cold and empty and glowing, as if it has been

10
00:00:16,272 --> 00:00:18,619
waiting all winter to get back to work.

11
00:00:19,281 --> 00:00:20,588
The shelves are exactly

12
00:00:20,588 --> 00:00:22,468
how you left them on day 30.

13
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:24,837
Gaps where you took the water.

14
00:00:24,837 --> 00:00:27,281
Tins pushed forward to hide the gaps.

15
00:00:27,281 --> 00:00:29,254
Under the shelf by the window,

16
00:00:29,254 --> 00:00:30,636
the little mark,

17
00:00:30,995 --> 00:00:34,105
a vertical line with a short stroke across it.

18
00:00:34,768 --> 00:00:37,254
Behind the counter, the drawer.

19
00:00:37,254 --> 00:00:38,584
Mara opens it.

20
00:00:38,584 --> 00:00:41,247
Inside, wrapped in a cloth,

21
00:00:41,247 --> 00:00:44,865
is the little entrance bell you took down on day five.

22
00:00:45,446 --> 00:00:46,632
She holds it for a long

23
00:00:46,632 --> 00:00:48,315
time without unwrapping it.

24
00:00:48,737 --> 00:00:49,741
In the staff room,

25
00:00:49,741 --> 00:00:53,084
the flattened cartons are still taped over the window.

26
00:00:53,084 --> 00:00:54,797
Your two old corners are still there,

27
00:00:54,797 --> 00:00:56,169
one each side of the room,

28
00:00:56,169 --> 00:00:59,349
with the dents of two people who slept badly for a month.

29
00:00:59,802 --> 00:01:01,848
You find your phone in the bottom of your bag,

30
00:01:01,848 --> 00:01:03,328
dead since the first week.

31
00:01:03,328 --> 00:01:05,210
There's a charger behind the counter.

32
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:07,456
You plug it in, mostly as a joke.

33
00:01:07,456 --> 00:01:08,774
The screen lights up.

34
00:01:08,774 --> 00:01:09,433
No signal.

35
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:10,939
And on the screen,

36
00:01:10,939 --> 00:01:12,812
the last message you ever received.

37
00:01:12,812 --> 00:01:14,545
A delivery notification,

38
00:01:14,545 --> 00:01:17,312
for a package you're probably never going to receive.

39
00:01:17,312 --> 00:01:19,016
You leave it charging anyway.

40
00:01:19,016 --> 00:01:21,179
You walk back out under the canopy.

41
00:01:21,179 --> 00:01:23,937
Every pump display is lit, showing zeros.

42
00:01:23,937 --> 00:01:24,813
On the pavement,

43
00:01:24,813 --> 00:01:27,839
by the door, a small marker is glowing.

44
00:01:27,839 --> 00:01:30,756
Two circles, joined by a short line.

45
00:01:30,756 --> 00:01:33,201
The very first one they ever placed.

46
00:01:33,201 --> 00:01:35,037
One step away from it,

47
00:01:35,037 --> 00:01:37,050
lying on its side, there's a bicycle.

48
00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:39,152
And by the nearest pump,

49
00:01:39,152 --> 00:01:43,249
gray, faded, and a little swollen, there's a carton.

50
00:01:43,249 --> 00:01:44,129
Your milk is still

51
00:01:44,129 --> 00:01:45,587
sitting beside the pump.

52
00:01:45,929 --> 00:01:48,090
It has been for two hundred and ten days.

53
00:01:48,090 --> 00:01:50,300
You decide not to open it.

54
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:53,453
Mara unties the red can from her bag,

55
00:01:53,453 --> 00:01:55,133
carries it across the forecourt,

56
00:01:55,133 --> 00:01:56,961
and sets it down by the pump.

57
00:01:57,447 --> 00:01:59,714
Right where it stood on the first evening.

58
00:01:59,714 --> 00:02:02,085
Then she steps back and looks at it.

59
00:02:02,085 --> 00:02:03,432
It's back where it started.

60
00:02:03,432 --> 00:02:04,309
So are you.

61
00:02:04,827 --> 00:02:05,671
On day 213,

62
00:02:05,671 --> 00:02:08,416
you find out who turned the lights on.

63
00:02:08,416 --> 00:02:09,605
For two days,

64
00:02:09,605 --> 00:02:12,054
you've walked around the station looking for a reason.

65
00:02:12,054 --> 00:02:13,632
There's no generator.

66
00:02:13,632 --> 00:02:14,807
The power lines along

67
00:02:14,807 --> 00:02:16,443
the road are still down.

68
00:02:16,801 --> 00:02:18,909
Behind the shop, there's a gray metal

69
00:02:18,909 --> 00:02:21,201
box on the wall, the kind with a warning

70
00:02:21,201 --> 00:02:23,799
sign and a lock, where the power comes in.

71
00:02:24,415 --> 00:02:25,658
Standing beside it,

72
00:02:25,658 --> 00:02:28,302
so close it almost touches, is a unit.

73
00:02:28,302 --> 00:02:30,915
Tall, smooth, and dark.

74
00:02:31,483 --> 00:02:33,483
At its base, two circles glow.

75
00:02:33,483 --> 00:02:35,434
And from the circles,

76
00:02:35,434 --> 00:02:37,693
a thin line of pale light runs across the

77
00:02:37,693 --> 00:02:39,955
ground and into the bottom of the box.

78
00:02:39,955 --> 00:02:42,352
You stand there for a long time.

79
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:44,540
Mara stands next to you.

80
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:46,839
On day 18, you watched these things

81
00:02:46,839 --> 00:02:47,983
line the road at the bend,

82
00:02:47,983 --> 00:02:51,070
and thought they were building a route out of the city.

83
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:51,658
On day 42,

84
00:02:51,658 --> 00:02:54,559
you watched them lead people to the stadium.

85
00:02:54,559 --> 00:02:57,360
Now one of them is standing behind a gas station,

86
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,972
quietly running the fridge.

87
00:02:58,972 --> 00:03:00,584
You write it in the ledger.

88
00:03:00,584 --> 00:03:02,329
Somebody wanted the lights on.

89
00:03:02,329 --> 00:03:04,422
Mara adds a question underneath.

90
00:03:04,989 --> 00:03:05,481
For who?

91
00:03:05,481 --> 00:03:06,904
You don't have an answer.

92
00:03:06,904 --> 00:03:09,416
You do have a working electric kettle

93
00:03:09,416 --> 00:03:11,132
in the staff room, for the first time

94
00:03:11,132 --> 00:03:13,806
since the evening you tried to pay for milk.

95
00:03:13,806 --> 00:03:15,819
You make two cups of hot water,

96
00:03:15,819 --> 00:03:18,256
because that's all you have to put in them.

97
00:03:18,256 --> 00:03:21,775
It's the best hot water you've ever had.

98
00:03:21,775 --> 00:03:25,078
On day 216, Mara hangs the bell back up.

99
00:03:25,078 --> 00:03:27,034
She climbs on the counter,

100
00:03:27,034 --> 00:03:29,444
unwraps the cloth, and hooks the little bell

101
00:03:29,444 --> 00:03:32,045
back on its bracket above the door.

102
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:33,140
You ask her why.

103
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:35,054
She says that on day five,

104
00:03:35,054 --> 00:03:37,787
you took it down so nobody would hear you.

105
00:03:37,787 --> 00:03:40,140
This time, she wants to hear who's coming.

106
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:42,287
The first time the door moves,

107
00:03:42,287 --> 00:03:43,348
it gives a tiny,

108
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:46,103
cheerful ring, just to check it still can.

109
00:03:46,103 --> 00:03:49,050
It rings again that same afternoon.

110
00:03:49,423 --> 00:03:51,876
You're behind the counter, counting tins.

111
00:03:51,876 --> 00:03:53,415
Your hands go still.

112
00:03:53,415 --> 00:03:55,317
Somebody is coming in.

113
00:03:55,317 --> 00:03:57,915
Two people stand in the doorway.

114
00:03:57,915 --> 00:04:00,016
A woman, and a man with a backpack,

115
00:04:00,016 --> 00:04:02,432
thin and tired, blinking at the light.

116
00:04:02,432 --> 00:04:04,929
They followed the circles along the road,

117
00:04:04,929 --> 00:04:06,726
from somewhere beyond the city.

118
00:04:06,726 --> 00:04:08,432
They don't know why.

119
00:04:08,432 --> 00:04:10,257
They just knew the lights hadn't

120
00:04:10,257 --> 00:04:11,473
come on since winter,

121
00:04:11,473 --> 00:04:14,411
and now they had, and they all pointed here.

122
00:04:14,411 --> 00:04:17,026
You give them hot water and two tins.

123
00:04:17,026 --> 00:04:17,870
By evening,

124
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:20,554
the bell has rung four more times.

125
00:04:20,554 --> 00:04:22,836
By the next morning, eleven times.

126
00:04:22,836 --> 00:04:24,567
People come in pairs,

127
00:04:24,567 --> 00:04:27,032
mostly, along the road from the bend.

128
00:04:27,032 --> 00:04:28,213
Some carry bags.

129
00:04:28,213 --> 00:04:29,084
Some don't.

130
00:04:29,084 --> 00:04:32,236
All of them look at the lit pumps the

131
00:04:32,236 --> 00:04:34,137
way you looked at your first lit circle.

132
00:04:34,137 --> 00:04:34,925
And all of them,

133
00:04:34,925 --> 00:04:37,751
sooner or later, ask the same question.

134
00:04:37,751 --> 00:04:39,976
Do you know what happens next?

135
00:04:40,527 --> 00:04:43,948
You open the tin, and take out the ledger.

136
00:04:43,948 --> 00:04:47,442
On day 219, two familiar faces walk in.

137
00:04:47,442 --> 00:04:50,330
The bell rings, and Mara looks up,

138
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:52,197
and then she's around the counter so

139
00:04:52,197 --> 00:04:54,582
fast she knocks a stack of tins over.

140
00:04:54,582 --> 00:04:55,642
The younger pair from

141
00:04:55,642 --> 00:04:57,339
the schoolhouse on the hill.

142
00:04:57,649 --> 00:04:59,477
The woman in the yellow raincoat.

143
00:04:59,477 --> 00:05:01,067
The man in the red hat.

144
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:02,773
They followed the lights

145
00:05:02,773 --> 00:05:04,135
for twenty days to get here.

146
00:05:04,135 --> 00:05:06,386
The older couple stayed behind.

147
00:05:06,386 --> 00:05:07,603
They're in the cellar,

148
00:05:07,603 --> 00:05:09,728
with the hens, and the door shut.

149
00:05:10,103 --> 00:05:11,522
The young woman reminds Mara

150
00:05:11,522 --> 00:05:13,343
of what she said at the gate.

151
00:05:13,943 --> 00:05:14,728
Be there.

152
00:05:14,728 --> 00:05:15,827
So they came.

153
00:05:15,827 --> 00:05:18,124
That night, they sit with you in

154
00:05:18,124 --> 00:05:18,850
the staff room,

155
00:05:18,850 --> 00:05:22,253
where the cartons are still taped over the windows.

156
00:05:22,253 --> 00:05:25,195
They tell you that, on day 198,

157
00:05:25,195 --> 00:05:28,886
when every light in the country came on for three seconds,

158
00:05:28,886 --> 00:05:30,229
the older man stood in the

159
00:05:30,229 --> 00:05:33,268
playground and watched it, and didn't say a word.

160
00:05:33,268 --> 00:05:35,198
The next morning, he gave them a

161
00:05:35,198 --> 00:05:37,292
bag of eggs, and told them to go.

162
00:05:37,292 --> 00:05:40,587
He said somebody should see how it ends.

163
00:05:40,587 --> 00:05:41,987
They've brought what's left

164
00:05:41,987 --> 00:05:44,200
of the eggs, wrapped in a scarf.

165
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,309
They give you six.

166
00:05:45,309 --> 00:05:47,668
That night, in the staff room,

167
00:05:47,668 --> 00:05:49,854
under the cartons, you cook eggs in a

168
00:05:49,854 --> 00:05:52,044
pan on the little hot plate,

169
00:05:52,044 --> 00:05:54,587
and four people eat them with their fingers.

170
00:05:54,587 --> 00:05:56,683
It's the closest thing to a

171
00:05:56,683 --> 00:05:58,384
party the station has ever seen.

172
00:05:58,384 --> 00:06:00,373
Mara writes it in the ledger.

173
00:06:00,373 --> 00:06:01,798
We called out.

174
00:06:01,798 --> 00:06:02,842
They came.

175
00:06:02,842 --> 00:06:05,968
On day 222, you read the ledger out loud.

176
00:06:05,968 --> 00:06:06,704
There are thirty-four

177
00:06:06,704 --> 00:06:08,687
people at the station now.

178
00:06:08,687 --> 00:06:10,123
They sit on the forecourt,

179
00:06:10,123 --> 00:06:13,572
on the curb, on the steps, and on the floor of the shop,

180
00:06:13,572 --> 00:06:15,616
and you stand by the door and read.

181
00:06:15,616 --> 00:06:17,067
From the beginning.

182
00:06:17,067 --> 00:06:17,864
Two figures,

183
00:06:17,864 --> 00:06:20,597
blue stripe, scanner, circles.

184
00:06:20,597 --> 00:06:22,256
Forty minutes.

185
00:06:22,256 --> 00:06:23,338
Closed room.

186
00:06:23,338 --> 00:06:25,169
Safe behind the wall.

187
00:06:25,169 --> 00:06:27,427
People laugh at that one.

188
00:06:27,427 --> 00:06:28,104
You let them.

189
00:06:28,104 --> 00:06:30,438
You laughed at it too, eventually.

190
00:06:30,438 --> 00:06:31,751
It took about a hundred days.

191
00:06:31,751 --> 00:06:34,516
You read about the road that lights for people,

192
00:06:34,516 --> 00:06:36,389
and the stadium, and the seats.

193
00:06:36,389 --> 00:06:38,081
You read about the gap that

194
00:06:38,081 --> 00:06:39,988
was only wide enough for one.

195
00:06:39,988 --> 00:06:42,724
Mara shows them the plain figure's drawings,

196
00:06:42,724 --> 00:06:43,604
one by one.

197
00:06:43,604 --> 00:06:46,766
The ship, full of tiny joined circles.

198
00:06:47,125 --> 00:06:48,631
The arrow, up.

199
00:06:48,631 --> 00:06:50,036
The sixty lines.

200
00:06:50,036 --> 00:06:51,221
The arrow,

201
00:06:51,221 --> 00:06:53,647
down, pointing at a small square.

202
00:06:53,647 --> 00:06:56,360
Someone asks what the square is.

203
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:57,847
You point at the floor.

204
00:06:57,847 --> 00:06:59,942
Nobody says anything for a while.

205
00:06:59,942 --> 00:07:01,653
Then a man near the back asks

206
00:07:01,653 --> 00:07:03,855
the only question that matters.

207
00:07:03,855 --> 00:07:06,226
If you've been watching them

208
00:07:06,226 --> 00:07:07,321
for two hundred and twenty-two days,

209
00:07:07,321 --> 00:07:09,064
what do you think they want?

210
00:07:09,064 --> 00:07:11,063
You've thought about that

211
00:07:11,063 --> 00:07:12,533
every day since the first one.

212
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:13,576
You give him the most

213
00:07:13,576 --> 00:07:15,248
honest answer in the ledger.

214
00:07:15,248 --> 00:07:16,359
You don't know.

215
00:07:16,359 --> 00:07:19,123
But nobody you know of has ever been hurt.

216
00:07:19,123 --> 00:07:20,658
And the only one you ever

217
00:07:20,658 --> 00:07:23,758
really got to know waved goodbye.

218
00:07:23,758 --> 00:07:26,863
On day 225, there are eighty-two people.

219
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:27,714
Mostly pairs,

220
00:07:27,714 --> 00:07:31,084
a few families, one baby, and you counted every one.

221
00:07:31,084 --> 00:07:32,215
The station has power,

222
00:07:32,215 --> 00:07:34,056
but it doesn't have water.

223
00:07:34,056 --> 00:07:35,549
The tap stopped on day eight,

224
00:07:35,549 --> 00:07:37,386
and the lights didn't fix that.

225
00:07:37,386 --> 00:07:39,110
So you do what you did

226
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:40,403
at the hardware store.

227
00:07:40,403 --> 00:07:41,191
You organize.

228
00:07:41,191 --> 00:07:42,686
Every bucket, barrel,

229
00:07:42,686 --> 00:07:45,172
and bin in the station goes under a gutter.

230
00:07:45,172 --> 00:07:47,216
When it rains on day 226,

231
00:07:47,216 --> 00:07:50,025
the whole forecourt fills them,

232
00:07:50,025 --> 00:07:52,542
and eighty-two people boil water in turns,

233
00:07:52,542 --> 00:07:54,295
in your kettle and four others.

234
00:07:54,813 --> 00:07:56,241
Food goes into one pile,

235
00:07:56,241 --> 00:07:58,767
behind the counter, and Mara writes every

236
00:07:58,767 --> 00:08:00,753
tin into a new column on the roll,

237
00:08:00,753 --> 00:08:03,196
the way you once wrote down hers.

238
00:08:03,196 --> 00:08:03,828
Eighty-two people,

239
00:08:03,828 --> 00:08:06,419
and the arithmetic still has to work.

240
00:08:06,419 --> 00:08:08,093
You see some of them looking at you the

241
00:08:08,093 --> 00:08:10,716
way you once looked at the bend in the road.

242
00:08:10,716 --> 00:08:12,297
As if you know where it goes.

243
00:08:12,297 --> 00:08:13,177
You don't.

244
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:15,638
You just wrote everything down.

245
00:08:15,638 --> 00:08:17,550
One evening, a boy of about

246
00:08:17,550 --> 00:08:19,703
ten asks if he can see the ledger.

247
00:08:19,703 --> 00:08:21,548
You give it to him.

248
00:08:21,548 --> 00:08:22,986
He reads it for an hour,

249
00:08:22,986 --> 00:08:25,642
very seriously, and then hands it back and

250
00:08:25,642 --> 00:08:28,112
tells you your handwriting is terrible.

251
00:08:28,112 --> 00:08:30,556
Mara says he's the first person

252
00:08:30,556 --> 00:08:31,871
in two hundred days who's been

253
00:08:31,871 --> 00:08:34,115
completely right about something.

254
00:08:34,570 --> 00:08:37,075
At night, people sleep everywhere.

255
00:08:37,075 --> 00:08:38,327
In the shop,

256
00:08:38,327 --> 00:08:40,878
under the canopy, in cars on the road.

257
00:08:40,878 --> 00:08:43,405
You and Mara sleep in the staff room,

258
00:08:43,405 --> 00:08:44,064
in the same two

259
00:08:44,064 --> 00:08:46,266
corners you slept in at the start.

260
00:08:46,266 --> 00:08:47,251
It feels smaller.

261
00:08:47,251 --> 00:08:49,739
It feels like a place you used to live.

262
00:08:50,128 --> 00:08:52,113
On day 228, you and Mara have

263
00:08:52,113 --> 00:08:54,676
the worst argument of your lives.

264
00:08:54,676 --> 00:08:55,641
It starts quietly,

265
00:08:55,641 --> 00:08:58,699
in the staff room, the way your arguments always do.

266
00:08:58,699 --> 00:09:01,393
Mara says she wants to see it land.

267
00:09:01,895 --> 00:09:03,245
You say you want to be

268
00:09:03,245 --> 00:09:04,595
far away when it does.

269
00:09:04,595 --> 00:09:07,421
She says the plain figure might be on it.

270
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:10,333
You say so might a thousand others,

271
00:09:10,333 --> 00:09:11,347
and none of them

272
00:09:11,347 --> 00:09:13,376
wiped your footprints off a hill.

273
00:09:13,376 --> 00:09:14,552
She says that's

274
00:09:14,552 --> 00:09:16,873
exactly why she wants to see.

275
00:09:16,873 --> 00:09:19,249
Then you say the thing you've

276
00:09:19,249 --> 00:09:20,937
been afraid to say since day 90.

277
00:09:20,937 --> 00:09:22,427
That if the gap is only wide

278
00:09:22,427 --> 00:09:24,698
enough for one, you think she'll take it.

279
00:09:25,249 --> 00:09:26,536
Mara goes very quiet.

280
00:09:26,536 --> 00:09:29,344
She takes out the roll and unrolls it,

281
00:09:29,344 --> 00:09:30,080
all the way,

282
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:32,710
until she finds her line from day 88.

283
00:09:33,212 --> 00:09:33,467
Two.

284
00:09:33,467 --> 00:09:34,999
Whatever happens.

285
00:09:34,999 --> 00:09:36,830
Underlined twice.

286
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,363
She asks if you think

287
00:09:38,363 --> 00:09:39,620
she wrote that as a joke.

288
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:40,890
You don't answer.

289
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:41,996
You don't have to.

290
00:09:41,996 --> 00:09:44,208
She writes one more word under it,

291
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:45,960
small, in the corner.

292
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,057
Together.

293
00:09:47,638 --> 00:09:49,866
Then she gives you the pencil, and waits.

294
00:09:49,866 --> 00:09:51,144
You underline it.

295
00:09:51,469 --> 00:09:53,024
You'll decide on the day.

296
00:09:53,024 --> 00:09:53,801
Both of you.

297
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:57,207
Whatever you do, you'll do it as two.

298
00:09:57,207 --> 00:10:00,422
On day 231, a new star appears.

299
00:10:00,422 --> 00:10:02,371
You notice it after dark,

300
00:10:02,371 --> 00:10:06,064
low over the city, where the ship hung for sixty days.

301
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:08,263
It's brighter than the others.

302
00:10:08,263 --> 00:10:09,297
It doesn't twinkle.

303
00:10:09,297 --> 00:10:10,817
You point it out to Mara,

304
00:10:10,817 --> 00:10:12,519
and she points it out to the young woman

305
00:10:12,519 --> 00:10:14,109
in the yellow raincoat,

306
00:10:14,109 --> 00:10:15,588
and within an hour,

307
00:10:15,588 --> 00:10:19,254
eighty-two people are standing on the forecourt looking at it.

308
00:10:19,254 --> 00:10:21,248
The next night, it's bigger.

309
00:10:21,655 --> 00:10:22,894
You check the old map,

310
00:10:22,894 --> 00:10:24,809
and the back of the receipt roll,

311
00:10:24,809 --> 00:10:27,142
and do the math the slow way.

312
00:10:27,142 --> 00:10:27,643
Eight days.

313
00:10:27,643 --> 00:10:29,421
The night after that,

314
00:10:29,421 --> 00:10:31,308
it isn't a point anymore.

315
00:10:31,308 --> 00:10:32,324
It has edges.

316
00:10:32,324 --> 00:10:33,925
Straight ones.

317
00:10:33,925 --> 00:10:35,653
Nobody sleeps much after that.

318
00:10:35,653 --> 00:10:37,997
People sit in pairs on the forecourt,

319
00:10:37,997 --> 00:10:40,108
wrapped in blankets, and watch it grow.

320
00:10:40,108 --> 00:10:41,956
Some of them hold hands.

321
00:10:41,956 --> 00:10:43,631
Some of them pack and unpack

322
00:10:43,631 --> 00:10:45,852
the same bag, over and over.

323
00:10:45,852 --> 00:10:47,339
You recognize that.

324
00:10:47,339 --> 00:10:48,974
You did it on day 24.

325
00:10:48,974 --> 00:10:50,144
What you carry.

326
00:10:50,144 --> 00:10:50,980
What stays.

327
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:53,642
You find yourself doing it too,

328
00:10:53,642 --> 00:10:56,483
with the gray bag, on the floor of the staff room.

329
00:10:56,483 --> 00:10:59,255
The ledger, the map, the pencil.

330
00:10:59,255 --> 00:11:00,310
The lantern.

331
00:11:00,310 --> 00:11:02,223
The marker in its cloth.

332
00:11:02,223 --> 00:11:04,245
You leave the bag packed.

333
00:11:04,923 --> 00:11:08,136
On day 234, the units come.

334
00:11:08,136 --> 00:11:11,320
You wake to a sound you've never heard.

335
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,798
It's the absence of sound, moving.

336
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:15,291
From every direction,

337
00:11:15,291 --> 00:11:17,878
along the roads, across the fields,

338
00:11:17,878 --> 00:11:20,429
the units are gliding toward the station.

339
00:11:20,787 --> 00:11:21,343
Tall,

340
00:11:21,343 --> 00:11:25,766
smooth, dark, a hand's width above the ground.

341
00:11:25,766 --> 00:11:26,316
Silent.

342
00:11:26,316 --> 00:11:27,415
Dozens of them.

343
00:11:27,415 --> 00:11:28,745
Then hundreds.

344
00:11:29,232 --> 00:11:30,555
They stop, one by one,

345
00:11:30,555 --> 00:11:34,409
at a distance from the station, and their circles light.

346
00:11:34,409 --> 00:11:36,924
By noon, they stand in a ring.

347
00:11:36,924 --> 00:11:37,723
A huge ring,

348
00:11:37,723 --> 00:11:39,690
all the way around the station,

349
00:11:39,690 --> 00:11:42,543
the road, the bend, and the field behind it.

350
00:11:42,543 --> 00:11:43,703
You climb onto the

351
00:11:43,703 --> 00:11:45,485
canopy roof to see it all.

352
00:11:45,485 --> 00:11:46,421
It's the mast.

353
00:11:46,421 --> 00:11:47,658
It's the park.

354
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,216
It's the bend in the frozen river.

355
00:11:50,216 --> 00:11:53,088
Except this time, you're inside it.

356
00:11:53,088 --> 00:11:54,085
Everyone is.

357
00:11:54,085 --> 00:11:55,906
You think of the

358
00:11:55,906 --> 00:11:57,694
drawing from day 154.

359
00:11:57,694 --> 00:12:00,637
Whatever is inside a ring goes up.

360
00:12:00,637 --> 00:12:01,478
So you test it,

361
00:12:01,478 --> 00:12:03,249
because that's who you are.

362
00:12:03,656 --> 00:12:05,529
You walk out to the nearest unit,

363
00:12:05,529 --> 00:12:08,071
and put your hand flat on its side.

364
00:12:08,071 --> 00:12:08,812
It's cold,

365
00:12:08,812 --> 00:12:12,071
and perfectly smooth, like a stone from a river.

366
00:12:12,071 --> 00:12:13,489
The circles at its base

367
00:12:13,489 --> 00:12:15,453
glow a little brighter.

368
00:12:15,453 --> 00:12:16,522
You step past it,

369
00:12:16,522 --> 00:12:19,554
out of the ring, onto the grass of the field.

370
00:12:19,863 --> 00:12:21,099
Nothing happens.

371
00:12:21,099 --> 00:12:22,116
Nobody comes.

372
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:24,242
You stand there for a minute,

373
00:12:24,242 --> 00:12:25,679
outside, in the wind.

374
00:12:25,679 --> 00:12:27,615
Then you step back in.

375
00:12:27,615 --> 00:12:28,589
People start asking

376
00:12:28,589 --> 00:12:29,855
you if they should leave.

377
00:12:29,855 --> 00:12:31,506
You tell them the truth.

378
00:12:31,506 --> 00:12:33,388
The units don't stop anyone walking.

379
00:12:33,388 --> 00:12:35,580
The lights don't hold anyone in.

380
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:37,312
You've crossed them yourself.

381
00:12:37,312 --> 00:12:38,179
Nobody leaves.

382
00:12:38,179 --> 00:12:39,905
They came here on purpose.

383
00:12:39,905 --> 00:12:40,637
You realize,

384
00:12:40,637 --> 00:12:45,323
climbing back onto the canopy roof, that you did too.

385
00:12:45,323 --> 00:12:48,765
On day 237, you do the last inventory.

386
00:12:48,765 --> 00:12:49,724
It's a habit.

387
00:12:49,724 --> 00:12:51,527
Some habits are earned.

388
00:12:51,527 --> 00:12:54,144
In your own bag, twelve tins.

389
00:12:54,144 --> 00:12:55,338
One bag of rice.

390
00:12:55,338 --> 00:12:56,851
Half a jar of jam.

391
00:12:56,851 --> 00:12:58,106
Two lighters.

392
00:12:58,545 --> 00:13:00,396
Two boxes of matches.

393
00:13:00,396 --> 00:13:02,898
And one very old match,

394
00:13:02,898 --> 00:13:05,845
in your pocket, from a cupboard on a narrowboat.

395
00:13:06,203 --> 00:13:08,058
Mara counts the ledger instead.

396
00:13:08,448 --> 00:13:10,747
Two hundred and thirty-seven days of it.

397
00:13:10,747 --> 00:13:13,193
Rolled so tight it

398
00:13:13,193 --> 00:13:14,550
barely fits in the tin.

399
00:13:14,550 --> 00:13:17,027
Longer than both your arms together.

400
00:13:17,027 --> 00:13:17,809
Three authors.

401
00:13:17,809 --> 00:13:19,727
You sit in the staff room,

402
00:13:19,727 --> 00:13:21,501
with the door open,

403
00:13:21,501 --> 00:13:24,131
because there's no point closing it anymore.

404
00:13:24,131 --> 00:13:25,964
The star isn't a star now.

405
00:13:25,964 --> 00:13:29,120
It covers a piece of the sky as big as

406
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:31,044
your hand at arm's length,

407
00:13:31,044 --> 00:13:35,624
dark, with straight edges, and it gets bigger every hour.

408
00:13:36,078 --> 00:13:37,757
Out on the forecourt,

409
00:13:37,757 --> 00:13:41,381
by the pump, the red can stands where it began.

410
00:13:41,381 --> 00:13:43,916
Two strips of tape on its handle.

411
00:13:44,337 --> 00:13:45,684
Your 61.

412
00:13:45,684 --> 00:13:46,786
Its 91.

413
00:13:46,786 --> 00:13:49,119
Mara says that if the plain

414
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:51,614
figure is coming, it'll know that can.

415
00:13:52,196 --> 00:13:54,853
You say it'll know the bicycle too.

416
00:13:55,339 --> 00:13:56,427
And the milk.

417
00:13:56,427 --> 00:13:57,282
She laughs,

418
00:13:57,282 --> 00:13:59,653
for the first time in three days.

419
00:13:59,653 --> 00:14:01,691
Then she goes quiet again,

420
00:14:01,691 --> 00:14:04,546
and leans her head against the wall.

421
00:14:04,546 --> 00:14:07,088
She says she's not scared of it landing.

422
00:14:07,463 --> 00:14:09,155
She's scared of it landing,

423
00:14:09,155 --> 00:14:10,959
and nobody getting out.

424
00:14:11,462 --> 00:14:12,961
You don't say anything.

425
00:14:12,961 --> 00:14:15,198
You're scared of the opposite.

426
00:14:15,814 --> 00:14:16,922
Before you sleep,

427
00:14:16,922 --> 00:14:20,904
Mara takes the pencil one more time, and writes the last

428
00:14:20,904 --> 00:14:23,228
line on the roll, at the very end,

429
00:14:23,667 --> 00:14:26,522
after the three authors and the sixty lines.

430
00:14:27,122 --> 00:14:28,121
Day 240.

431
00:14:28,121 --> 00:14:31,486
She draws a box around it,

432
00:14:31,486 --> 00:14:33,288
like you did with 180.

433
00:14:33,288 --> 00:14:35,518
Then, after a moment,

434
00:14:35,518 --> 00:14:38,829
she draws two small circles beside it,

435
00:14:38,829 --> 00:14:41,286
joined by a short line.

436
00:14:41,286 --> 00:14:44,484
On day 239, the marker begins to glow.

437
00:14:44,484 --> 00:14:46,580
You notice it at midnight,

438
00:14:46,580 --> 00:14:48,040
when you can't sleep.

439
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:48,969
A pale light,

440
00:14:48,969 --> 00:14:51,900
leaking from the edges of the tin lid.

441
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:53,171
You open it.

442
00:14:53,625 --> 00:14:54,926
Inside, in its cloth,

443
00:14:54,926 --> 00:14:57,356
the marker from the ice is glowing.

444
00:14:57,874 --> 00:15:00,534
Two circles, joined by a short line.

445
00:15:00,534 --> 00:15:04,091
The first light it has made since day 180.

446
00:15:04,769 --> 00:15:06,534
You hold it in your hand.

447
00:15:06,534 --> 00:15:07,281
It's warm.

448
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,886
Mara sits up in her corner,

449
00:15:08,886 --> 00:15:10,985
and you show it to her without a word.

450
00:15:11,439 --> 00:15:13,118
On the very first night,

451
00:15:13,118 --> 00:15:16,140
a figure placed a marker exactly like this on

452
00:15:16,140 --> 00:15:17,474
the pavement outside,

453
00:15:17,474 --> 00:15:20,105
and moved a bicycle one step away from it,

454
00:15:20,105 --> 00:15:22,906
and you didn't understand the difference.

455
00:15:22,906 --> 00:15:25,111
You still don't understand everything.

456
00:15:25,111 --> 00:15:26,975
But you understand that one.

457
00:15:26,975 --> 00:15:28,316
Already counted.

458
00:15:28,316 --> 00:15:29,781
Leave these two.

459
00:15:30,126 --> 00:15:32,130
You don't know if it means that tomorrow.

460
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:33,418
You don't know if it means

461
00:15:33,418 --> 00:15:35,565
anything at all to whoever's coming.

462
00:15:35,565 --> 00:15:36,638
But it's glowing.

463
00:15:36,638 --> 00:15:37,970
And somebody,

464
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:41,870
somewhere above you, knows exactly where you are.

465
00:15:41,870 --> 00:15:43,351
You put it in your pocket,

466
00:15:43,351 --> 00:15:44,912
next to the old match.

467
00:15:45,511 --> 00:15:46,188
Outside,

468
00:15:46,188 --> 00:15:50,710
under the canopy, eighty-two people sit awake, and nobody talks.

469
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:53,417
Above them, the dark shape with

470
00:15:53,417 --> 00:15:56,256
straight edges fills a quarter of the sky.

471
00:15:56,256 --> 00:15:57,482
On day 240,

472
00:15:57,482 --> 00:15:59,418
you're standing at the payment machine.

473
00:15:59,418 --> 00:16:00,686
You don't know why.

474
00:16:01,253 --> 00:16:03,600
It's early, and everyone else is outside,

475
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,357
on the forecourt, looking up.

476
00:16:05,357 --> 00:16:07,091
The machine has been lit since

477
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:08,955
the night you came back,

478
00:16:08,955 --> 00:16:11,229
its little screen still asking for payment,

479
00:16:11,229 --> 00:16:13,027
as if nothing ever happened.

480
00:16:13,369 --> 00:16:15,148
You put your hand in your pocket,

481
00:16:15,148 --> 00:16:16,580
past the old match,

482
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,199
and find something soft and folded.

483
00:16:19,199 --> 00:16:20,407
A crumpled bill.

484
00:16:20,407 --> 00:16:22,661
The one you were trying to pay with,

485
00:16:22,661 --> 00:16:25,273
on the evening it all started.

486
00:16:25,273 --> 00:16:26,354
Two hundred and forty days,

487
00:16:26,354 --> 00:16:28,333
in the same pocket.

488
00:16:28,333 --> 00:16:30,687
You smooth it out against your knee.

489
00:16:31,109 --> 00:16:32,603
You feed it into the slot.

490
00:16:32,603 --> 00:16:34,721
The machine thinks about it.

491
00:16:34,721 --> 00:16:35,953
Then it takes it.

492
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:37,895
A small, cheerful beep.

493
00:16:38,332 --> 00:16:40,125
Mara, in the doorway,

494
00:16:40,125 --> 00:16:44,489
starts laughing so hard she has to hold on to the frame.

495
00:16:44,489 --> 00:16:46,291
And then the sky changes.

496
00:16:46,728 --> 00:16:47,875
Every shadow on the

497
00:16:47,875 --> 00:16:49,896
forecourt disappears at once.

498
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:52,206
You don't look for storm clouds.

499
00:16:52,206 --> 00:16:53,341
You know what has a

500
00:16:53,341 --> 00:16:54,932
perfectly straight edge.

501
00:16:54,932 --> 00:16:57,383
The ship slides over the station,

502
00:16:57,383 --> 00:16:58,361
silent,

503
00:16:58,361 --> 00:17:02,058
enormous, filling the sky from the bend to the field.

504
00:17:02,671 --> 00:17:03,655
Eighty-two people stand

505
00:17:03,655 --> 00:17:05,983
under it and don't make a sound.

506
00:17:06,534 --> 00:17:07,945
Somewhere at the back,

507
00:17:07,945 --> 00:17:12,341
a baby starts to cry, and somebody hushes it, gently.

508
00:17:12,341 --> 00:17:13,599
A smaller shape

509
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:16,006
separates from its underside.

510
00:17:16,006 --> 00:17:18,721
It settles onto the road without wheels,

511
00:17:18,721 --> 00:17:19,640
without smoke,

512
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,698
without anything you recognize as an engine.

513
00:17:23,313 --> 00:17:25,027
Two figures step out.

514
00:17:25,027 --> 00:17:27,274
Smooth pale green faces.

515
00:17:27,648 --> 00:17:28,714
Black eyes.

516
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:30,967
Sealed dark uniforms.

517
00:17:31,502 --> 00:17:34,227
One has a blue stripe across its shoulder.

518
00:17:34,227 --> 00:17:37,034
The other carries a flat metal case.

519
00:17:37,034 --> 00:17:38,813
The crowd parts around them.

520
00:17:38,813 --> 00:17:40,668
They walk past the bicycle.

521
00:17:40,668 --> 00:17:41,989
Past the milk.

522
00:17:42,411 --> 00:17:43,488
Past the red can,

523
00:17:43,488 --> 00:17:46,449
by the pump, with two numbers on its handle.

524
00:17:46,967 --> 00:17:48,525
The plain figure stops

525
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:50,287
in front of you and Mara.

526
00:17:50,287 --> 00:17:51,996
It looks at you.

527
00:17:51,996 --> 00:17:52,596
At her.

528
00:17:52,596 --> 00:17:53,795
Then it kneels,

529
00:17:53,795 --> 00:17:57,753
and opens its case, and sets a marker down on the pavement,

530
00:17:57,753 --> 00:17:59,123
right at your feet.

531
00:17:59,658 --> 00:18:00,745
You look down.

532
00:18:00,745 --> 00:18:02,773
It isn't two circles.

533
00:18:02,773 --> 00:18:03,616
It's three.

534
00:18:03,616 --> 00:18:04,796
Three circles,

535
00:18:04,796 --> 00:18:08,375
in a row, joined by two short lines.

536
00:18:08,375 --> 00:18:11,331
In your pocket, the old marker is so

537
00:18:11,331 --> 00:18:14,689
warm you can feel it through the cloth.

538
00:18:14,689 --> 00:18:15,889
For two hundred and forty days,

539
00:18:15,889 --> 00:18:17,784
they've come in pairs.

540
00:18:17,784 --> 00:18:20,112
Once, there was only one.

541
00:18:20,112 --> 00:18:20,905
Never three.

542
00:18:20,905 --> 00:18:23,144
Mara takes your hand.

543
00:18:23,503 --> 00:18:24,849
The plain figure stays

544
00:18:24,849 --> 00:18:26,196
kneeling at your feet,

545
00:18:26,196 --> 00:18:29,806
its case open, looking up at the two of you.

546
00:18:29,806 --> 00:18:30,496
Waiting.

547
00:18:30,496 --> 00:18:31,466
On day one,

548
00:18:31,466 --> 00:18:33,643
you didn't understand the difference.

549
00:18:33,643 --> 00:18:35,406
This time, you have to.
